-- title:
--   Level automorphism acts on transported cusp data through γ
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ divisible by neither; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) with $H$ the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, let $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$, and let $\tau$ be an $L$-automorphism of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$: on every element of $K$ which is a ratio of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$, $\tau$ realises the substitution by the $(q\ell)$-conjugate of $\gamma^{-1}$ after transport to $\mathbb C$ by any such $\iota$. Further data: a variable change $C_0$ over $L((\mathsf q))$ whose $u$ satisfies $u\,(2x_{(1,0)}+\tfrac16)=2y_{(1,0)}+x_{(1,0)}$ for the cusp point at index $(1,0)$ and with $(r,s,t)=(-\tfrac1{12},-\tfrac12,\tfrac1{24})$; a unit $\mu$ of $K$ with $\mu\,(2y_v+x_v)\cdot 2(x_{(1,0)}+\tfrac1{12})=(2y_{(1,0)}+x_{(1,0)})\cdot 2(x_v+\tfrac1{12})$ for $v=(\gamma_{00},-\gamma_{10})\bmod q\ell$; a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $K$ whose base change to $L((\mathsf q))$ is $C_0\cdot\mathrm{tateBase}\,L\,(q\ell)$; a nonzero $n\in\mathbb Z/q\ell$; and level-$p$ data $D$ over $K$ whose base change is the $C_0$-variable change of the cusp data at indices $(n,0)$ and $(0,-n)$. The conclusion asserts, with $P=$ `toPoint` $W\,D.xP\,D.yP$ and $Q=$ `toPoint` $W\,D.xQ\,D.yQ$ (the affine point when nonsingular, and $0$ otherwise), that the pairs $(\mu^{-2}\tau(D.xP),\mu^{-3}\tau(D.yP))$ and $(\mu^{-2}\tau(D.xQ),\mu^{-3}\tau(D.yQ))$ are nonsingular points of the affine model of $W$, and that $\gamma_{00}P+\gamma_{10}Q$ and $\gamma_{01}P+\gamma_{11}Q$ equal the points determined by those two pairs respectively.
--
--   This is the identification of the action of a level automorphism on a $(q\ell)$-torsion basis transported from the Tate curve at a cusp: $\tau$, rescaled by the cocycle $\mu$, permutes the two marked points by the matrix $\gamma$ acting on indices. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.level_snd_fst_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.level_snd_fst_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_gamma0Pow) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_level_snd_snd_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_level_snd_snd_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_gamma0Pow) to compare the level structure with its relabelling under $\Gamma_0$.
